From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:52:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Align steering release fixtures with model initialization and
 GPU teardown

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354, after the
199-patch output-parser stack at 9dd408b8ee85.

The complete release gate exposed hand-built model/config objects missing
the downstream steering defaults, and module-scoped CPU import stubs that
remained installed during the real per-test GPU cleanup. Give stand-ins
the constructor defaults and restore host stubs before cleanup.

Quality: tests only; no serving source, weights, sampling or kernels change.
Tests: previous full GPU gate had 20 assertion failures and 30 teardown
errors in these five files. Corrected files pass 133 CPU cases, with 27
GPU-only skips; full GPU rerun remains required.
Upstream status: downstream test maintenance; not submitted upstream.
---
